.TH CRONTAB 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crontab \- gere les tables de cron / maintain crontab files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crontab
[-u user] (-l | -e | -r | file)
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs, lists (-l), edits (-e, with $VISUAL, $EDITOR or vi) or removes (-r) the crontab of a user. The table is kept in /var/spool/cron/crontabs/USER. Each
line has five fields (minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week) followed by the command; fields accept lists, ranges, steps (*/5), month and day names.
@reboot @hourly @daily @weekly @monthly @yearly replace the five fields. NAME=value lines set the job environment. In the command, % ends the command and the
rest becomes its standard input.
.SH SEE ALSO
crond(1), at(1)
